    "narrative": "The highlight of today\u2019s slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP is **Mickey Moniak**, who earns our highest score of 75.98. He benefits from an excellent matchup against Roki Sasaki, where a favorable park factor and a massive 14% platoon edge are amplified by the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, creating an ideal environment for **Mickey Moniak** to exploit his elite sprint speed for stolen base opportunities. Similarly, **Jose Caballero** (64.59) and **Isaac Paredes** (64.31) are elite starts; while **Jose Caballero** faces a tough strike-thrower in Chris Bassitt, his underlying park factors and our mandate to prioritize SB-threats keep him firmly in the green despite a lower-order lineup assignment. **Isaac Paredes** rounds out the top tier, as his strong platoon splits against the right-handed Walbert Ure\u00f1a make him a high-efficiency play for RBI production.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Austin Riley**, who scored a 54.15 and narrowly missed the cut. While **Austin Riley** offers legitimate power upside, he was edged out by players like **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Max Muncy** whose positional flexibility and higher daily floors proved more valuable in our current roster configuration. The optimizer also flagged a warning for **Corbin Carroll** (56.41); while he remains a start, his score is tempered by a daunting matchup against the left-handed Payton Tolle. Owners should monitor the lineup cards closely, as **Gabriel Moreno**, **Cole Young**, **Brice Turang**, **Griffin Conine**, and **Seiya Suzuki** all have their scores based on assumed order projections\u2014a significant swing factor if the managers slot them lower in the lineup than anticipated. Despite the volatility surrounding **Gabriel Moreno** and **Cole Young**, our core remains well-positioned to capitalize on the few available stolen base opportunities across the league today.",
